{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParityConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParityConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.convergence_not_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.convergence_not_derivation","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorWeightParityConvergence.lean#L49-L57","doc":"**Convergence, not derivation (the packaged statement).** For `A = k+1 ≥ 1`: the signs agree in\nvalue (`weight_parity_eq_cluster_sign`) while the weight order strictly exceeds the (even) deficit\norder — so the shared `(−1)^{A−1}` comes from distinct-order objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.weight_parity_eq_cluster_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.weight_parity_eq_cluster_sign","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorWeightParityConvergence.lean#L39-L47","doc":"**The parity coincidence.** The weight bar-sign `(−1)^{n-1} = (−1)^{3A−1}` equals the cluster sign\n`(−1)^{A−1}` (phrased with `A = k+1` so `ℕ`-subtraction is well-defined). Same VALUE — the source\norders differ (facts above), so this is a convergence, not a derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.weight_order_gt_deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.weight_order_gt_deficit","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorWeightParityConvergence.lean#L33-L37","doc":"**The weight prefactor is subleading.** For `A ≥ 1` the Ocneanu-weight order `n−1 = 3A−1` strictly\nexceeds the deficit order `2(A−1)`. Since `τ_A` is a normalized (link/unlink) ratio the weight\nprefactor cancels; being higher-order it cannot set the deficit's leading sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.deficit_order_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorWeightParity.deficit_order_even","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorWeightParityConvergence.lean#L28-L31","doc":"**Deficit order is even.** `2(A−1)` is even, so the A-body deficit `1 − τ_A` (leading order\n`h^{2(A−1)}`) is bar-even; its sign is a leading-*coefficient* effect, not a bar-parity flip. ","signatureChunk":0}]}